# Normalise line endings to LF, in the repository and in the working copy.
#
# Why: core.autocrlf=true gives Windows checkouts CRLF line endings. A JSX
# className attribute written across several lines then keeps the carriage
# return in the server-rendered HTML but not in the client render, and React
# reports it as a hydration mismatch ("some attributes of the server rendered
# HTML didn't match the client properties"). Checking out LF everywhere removes
# that whole class of bug rather than patching it one component at a time.
#
# Existing files keep their current endings until they are next checked out.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
